==Trivia==
*Goblins are small, grotesque, monstrous creatures that appear in the folklore of multiple European cultures. First attested in stories from the Middle Ages, they are ascribed conflicting abilities, temperaments, and appearances depending on the story and country of origin, ranging from mischievous household spirits to malicious, bestial thieves. They often have magical abilities similar to a fairy or demon, such as the ability to shapeshift. Similar creatures include [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Duende duendes], [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kobold kobolds], [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leprechaun leprechauns], and [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ghoul ghouls].
**In the Italian and Japanese language setting of the game, the Dart Goblin's name translates to "Blowgun Goblin". In the French, German, Spanish, Dutch, Norwegian. Arabic, Persian, Malaysian, and Vietnamese language setting of the game, the Dart Goblin's name translates to "Blowpipe Goblin", "Blowgun Kobold", "Dart-throwing Duende", "Blowpipe Kobold", "Blowing Goblin", "Arrow-blowing Ghoul", "Blowdart Goblin", "Greedy Goblin", and "Dart-throwing Leprechauns" respectively.
**The Dart Goblin is 1 of 17 [[cards]] associated with [[Goblins]], with the others being [[Spear Goblins]], [[Goblin Gang]], [[Baby Goblins]], [[Goblin Demolisher]], [[Suspicious Bush]], [[Goblin Cage]], [[Goblin Hut]], [[Goblin Giant]], [[Goblin Barrel]], [[Goblin Curse]], [[Goblin Drill]], [[Goblin Machine]], [[Party Rocket]], [[Party Hut]], [[Goblinstein]], and of course, Goblins.
*The Dart Goblin is making the practice of playing the [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Didgeridoo didgeridoo]. The didgeridoo is a wind instrument, played with vibrating lips to produce a continuous drone while using a special breathing technique called circular breathing. The didgeridoo was developed by Aboriginal peoples of northern Australia at least 1,000 years ago, and is now in use around the world, though still most strongly associated with Indigenous Australian music.
**In the Arabic language setting of the game, the Dart Goblin plays the oboe. In the Chinese language setting of the game, the Dart Goblin plays the flute.
*The Dart Goblin is one of the first [[:Category:Troop Cards|troop]] cards to receive a card render, alongside the [[Archers]], [[Knight]], [[Goblins]], [[Bomber]], [[Skeletons]], [[Barbarians]], [[Bats]], [[Royal Recruits]], [[Skeleton Barrel]], [[Rascals]], [[Musketeer]], [[Giant]], [[Valkyrie]], [[Wizard]], [[Flying Machine]], [[Hog Rider]], [[Royal Hogs]], [[Zappies]], [[Elixir Golem]], [[Baby Dragon]], [[Skeleton Army]], [[Witch]], [[P.E.K.K.A.|P.E.K.K.A]], [[Prince]], [[Balloon]], [[Giant Skeleton]], [[Goblin Giant]], [[Hunter]], [[Electro Dragon]], [[Wall Breakers]], [[Bowler]], [[Cannon Cart]], [[Mega Knight]], [[Ram Rider]], [[Miner]], [[Royal Ghost]], [[Ice Wizard]], [[Magic Archer]], [[Bandit]], [[Lava Hound]], [[Night Witch]], and [[Fisherman]].
*The Dart Goblin is the only troop that has been featured with a [[Buff#Poison Attack|Poison Attack]] [[buff]].
*In the card's description, "''Double Trouble gum''" is likely a reference to the brand of gum called [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dubble_Bubble Dubble Bubble].
*The Dart Goblin, along with the Minions, Bomber, Skeletons, [[Skeleton Dragons]], [[Ice Spirit]], [[Mini P.E.K.K.A.|Mini P.E.K.K.A]], [[Mega Minion]], [[Ice Golem]], Elixir Golem, [[Goblin Cage|Goblin Brawler]], [[Guards]], Baby Dragon, P.E.K.K.A, Giant Skeleton, [[Golem]], Wall Breakers, Bowler, [[Executioner]], Mega Knight, [[Inferno Dragon]], Royal Ghost, and Lava Hound, are featured as a [https://squad-busters.fandom.com/wiki/Monsters monster] in [https://squad-busters.fandom.com/wiki/Squad_Busters_Wiki Squad Busters].
*The Dart Goblin's C.H.A.O.S Common Modifier Speedy Goblinez is a reference to [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Speedy_Gonzales Speedy Gonzalez].
*The Dart Goblin is the subject of certain cosmetics in the game. More specifically:
**The Dart Goblin is the subject of 3 [[Emotes]].
**The Dart Goblin is the subject of 2 [[Battle Banners|Battle Banner]] items.
***The Dart Goblin is one of the first troops to be the subject of a Battle Banner item, along with the Mini P.E.K.K.A, P.E.K.K.A, Prince, Giant Skeleton, Mega Knight, [[Super Witch]], and the [[Golden Knight]].

